## Styling

- Tailwind CSS v4. `apps/web/src/styles/tokens.tailwind.css` binds the tokens with `@theme inline reference`, so `bg-page` reads `var(--color-page)` and `p-gutter` reads `var(--spacing-gutter)`. `apps/web/src/index.css` imports the UI package's `globals.css` first, then both token files.
- `packages/ui` holds the shadcn/ui components on Base UI, imported as `@{{name}}/ui/components/<name>`. Add one with `pnpm ui:add <name>` rather than writing it by hand. It runs the shadcn CLI in `packages/ui`, then `pnpm lint --fix` and `pnpm format`. The fixes only clear autofixable rules, so if lint makes it exit 1, fix what's left by hand, run `pnpm format` and confirm with `pnpm lint`. Don't count on the pre-commit hook here, as it lets warnings through. Without a terminal, shadcn stops at its overwrite prompt when a file it needs already exists, and exits 0 without the component. So check `packages/ui/src/components/<name>.tsx` exists afterwards. If it doesn't, run `yes n | pnpm ui:add <name> -y`, which keeps your existing files. `--overwrite` replaces them and drops local edits. The components keep shadcn's shape, so `oxlint.styling.ts` turns a few rules off for them.
